{
  "subtype": "focus_inference",
  "implied_focus": "Market-expansion potential of companies, characterized by industry sector, geographic location, and growth/maturity stage",
  "per_column": [
    {
      "name": "Industry_Focus",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Industry sector is a core dimension for assessing which markets/segments offer expansion opportunities; a data-inferable facet from company description."
    },
    {
      "name": "Geographic_Region",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Geographic region directly supports market-expansion analysis (where markets are concentrated or underserved); derivable from address/lat-long."
    },
    {
      "name": "Market_Expansion_Stage",
      "supports_focus": true,
      "rationale": "Maturity/growth stage is central to identifying expansion candidates and readiness; directly names the focus, though values are somewhat inconsistent (e.g., 'Growth Stage' vs 'Growth Stage Focus', 'Nonprofit', 'R&D Center' are off-taxonomy)."
    }
  ],
  "focus_coherence": 0.85,
  "structure_quality": 0.72,
  "focus_actionability": 0.8,
  "rationale": "The three columns converge coherently on a single implied focus: company market-expansion potential viewed through industry, geography, and maturity/growth stage. These are distinct, complementary facets at a useful granularity rather than a grab-bag or single restatement, so coherence and actionability are strong. Structure quality is dampened because Market_Expansion_Stage mixes conceptual dimensions (lifecycle stage, entity type like 'Nonprofit'/'R&D Center'/'Incubator', and a redundant 'Growth Stage Focus' duplicate), weakening it as a clean predictor facet. Overall the set genuinely proposes and structures an actionable focus, with minor taxonomic noise preventing top marks."
}

